{"op":"add","path":"/state/providers/0","value":{"id":"aws","name":"Amazon Web Services","rank":1,"tagline":"The default. Widest service catalog, deepest talent pool, most third-party integrations — and you will pay for the privilege.","share":"31%","regions":36,"zones":114,"sla":"99.99% (multi-AZ)","launched":2006,"services":"240+","price":"$147","egress":"$0.09/GB, 100 GB/mo free","cold":"~120–350 ms (Lambda, Node)","free":"12-mo trial + generous always-free","supportEntry":"$29/mo Developer","compliance":"143+","score":91,"strength":"If a managed service exists anywhere, it exists here first. Best IAM model, best marketplace, best hiring pool, Graviton gives real 20–40% price/perf wins.","weakness":"Egress is expensive, the console is a maze, and cost governance requires real discipline (or a FinOps hire)."}}
{"op":"add","path":"/state/providers/1","value":{"id":"gcp","name":"Google Cloud Platform","rank":2,"tagline":"Best developer experience of the big three, best data/AI stack, best Kubernetes — narrower catalog everywhere else.","share":"12%","regions":41,"zones":127,"sla":"99.99% (regional)","launched":2008,"services":"150+","price":"$142 (≈$99 w/ CUD)","egress":"$0.12/GB premium tier, 200 GB/mo free","cold":"~100–300 ms (Cloud Run)","free":"$300/90-day credit + strong always-free","supportEntry":"$29/mo + 3% Standard","compliance":"110+","score":88,"strength":"BigQuery has no true equivalent anywhere. GKE Autopilot and Cloud Run are the least painful way to ship containers. Automatic sustained-use discounts, live-migration VMs, global VPC.","weakness":"Premium-tier egress is the priciest of the five, enterprise support is expensive, and Google's product-deprecation reputation still scares CTOs."}}
{"op":"add","path":"/state/providers/2","value":{"id":"azure","name":"Microsoft Azure","rank":3,"tagline":"The enterprise incumbent's cloud. Unbeatable if you already own Windows Server, SQL Server, AD and E5 licences.","share":"25%","regions":60,"zones":"170+ DCs","sla":"99.99% (AZ VMs)","launched":2010,"services":"200+","price":"$140","egress":"$0.087/GB, 100 GB/mo free","cold":"~200 ms–1.5 s (Functions Consumption)","free":"$200/30-day credit + 12-mo + always-free","supportEntry":"$29/mo Developer","compliance":"100+ (largest portfolio claim)","score":87,"strength":"Hybrid story (Arc, Stack HCI) is genuinely best-in-class. Entra ID is the enterprise identity standard. Hybrid Benefit + EA discounts can cut Windows/SQL costs by 40–85%. First-party OpenAI models.","weakness":"Most outage-prone of the big three in recent years, portal performance is inconsistent, and quota/region capacity errors are a common surprise."}}
{"op":"add","path":"/state/providers/3","value":{"id":"oci","name":"Oracle Cloud Infrastructure","rank":4,"tagline":"The price disruptor. Absurdly cheap egress and Arm compute, plus the only free tier you can actually run production side-projects on.","share":"3%","regions":50,"zones":"1–3 AD/region","sla":"99.99% + perf & manageability SLAs","launched":2016,"services":"100+","price":"$47 (Ampere A1)","egress":"10 TB/mo free, then $0.0085/GB","cold":"~1–3 s (OCI Functions)","free":"Always-free 4 Ampere OCPUs / 24 GB RAM + 200 GB storage + $300 credit","supportEntry":"24/7 support included with paid accounts","compliance":"80+","score":83,"strength":"Egress is ~10x cheaper than AWS/Azure and 14x cheaper than GCP premium. Uniform per-region pricing worldwide. Only cloud offering performance and manageability SLAs, not just availability. Best Oracle DB / Exadata by definition.","weakness":"Thin managed-service catalog, small third-party ecosystem, few engineers have it on their CV, fewer AZs per region, and serverless is clearly a generation behind."}}
