{"op":"add","path":"/state/steps/0","value":{"id":"s1","order":1,"title":"Activate your company account","category":"Identity","eta":"10 min","description":"Claim your SSO identity so every other tool can recognise you.","detail":"Open the activation email sent to your personal address, sign in at id.acme.com with the one-time code, then set your permanent password (16+ characters). Confirm your display name and pronouns while you're there.","done":true}}
{"op":"add","path":"/state/steps/1","value":{"id":"s2","order":2,"title":"Install the password manager","category":"Security","eta":"10 min","description":"1Password is the only approved place to store work credentials.","detail":"Install 1Password from Self Service, join the Acme vault with the invite link, and enable browser autofill. Move any work logins you already created out of your browser's saved passwords.","done":true}}
{"op":"add","path":"/state/steps/2","value":{"id":"s3","order":3,"title":"Turn on 2FA with your security key","category":"Security","eta":"10 min","description":"Two factors on SSO, GitHub, and the admin console.","detail":"Register the YubiKey from your welcome box as your primary factor and your phone authenticator as backup. Print or store the recovery codes in 1Password, never in a notes app.","done":false}}
{"op":"add","path":"/state/steps/3","value":{"id":"s4","order":4,"title":"Connect to the VPN","category":"Network","eta":"15 min","description":"Required for internal dashboards, staging, and the wiki.","detail":"Install Tailscale from Self Service, sign in with SSO, and accept the device key. Verify access by loading wiki.internal.acme.com — if it times out, switch off any personal VPN first.","done":false}}
{"op":"add","path":"/state/steps/4","value":{"id":"s5","order":5,"title":"Verify laptop disk encryption","category":"Device","eta":"10 min","description":"FileVault (macOS) or BitLocker (Windows) must report Enabled.","detail":"macOS: System Settings → Privacy & Security → FileVault. Windows: Settings → Privacy & security → Device encryption. Escrow the recovery key to IT when prompted — the compliance check runs nightly.","done":false}}
{"op":"add","path":"/state/steps/5","value":{"id":"s6","order":6,"title":"Enrol your device in MDM","category":"Device","eta":"10 min","description":"Lets IT push security patches without touching your files.","detail":"Open the Company Portal app and complete enrolment. You should see a green 'Compliant' badge and the approved app catalogue within a few minutes.","done":false}}
{"op":"add","path":"/state/steps/6","value":{"id":"s7","order":7,"title":"Join your team channels","category":"Collaboration","eta":"5 min","description":"Slack, calendar invites, and the on-call rota.","detail":"Request access to #design-team, #product-releases, #it-helpdesk, and #acme-general. Accept the recurring standup and sprint review invites, then set your Slack profile photo and working hours.","done":false}}
{"op":"add","path":"/state/steps/7","value":{"id":"s8","order":8,"title":"Complete the security awareness module","category":"Compliance","eta":"20 min","description":"Due within your first five days — do it now while you're set up.","detail":"Launch the 'Phishing & Data Handling' course from the learning portal. Passing score is 80%; your certificate files automatically against your onboarding ticket.","done":false}}
{"op":"add","path":"/elements/tips","value":{"type":"Card","props":{"title":"Common first-day snags","description":"Check here before opening a ticket."},"children":["tips-accordion"]}}
{"op":"add","path":"/elements/tips-accordion","value":{"type":"Accordion","props":{"type":"single","items":[{"title":"My activation code expired","content":"Codes last 24 hours. Request a new one at id.acme.com/activate using your work email, or ask your IT buddy to re-issue it from the admin console."},{"title":"VPN connects but internal sites won't load","content":"Disable other VPNs and custom DNS, then reconnect. If wiki.internal.acme.com still fails, confirm your device shows Compliant in Company Portal — non-compliant devices are blocked from internal routes."},{"title":"FileVault says it's still encrypting","content":"That's fine. Encryption finishes in the background, usually within an hour. You can keep working; just leave the laptop plugged in."},{"title":"I can't find a team channel","content":"Private channels need an invite. Ask your manager to add you, or post your team name in #it-helpdesk and we'll route the request."}]},"children":[]}}
