{"op":"add","path":"/state/steps/0","value":{"id":"activate","number":1,"title":"Activate your corporate account","tool":"Okta SSO","minutes":10,"done":true,"description":"Claim your username (p.raghunathan@northwind.io) and set your first password using the activation link IT emailed to your personal address.","detail":"Open the activation email titled 'Welcome to Northwind — activate your account'. The link expires 72 hours after your start date. Choose a passphrase of at least 14 characters; you'll replace it with a manager-generated one in Step 2. If the link has expired, request a new one from the helpdesk portal rather than resetting yourself.","owner":"IT Identity team","contact":"#it-helpdesk","guide":"https://it.northwind.io/guides/account-activation"}}
{"op":"add","path":"/state/steps/1","value":{"id":"password-manager","number":2,"title":"Install and unlock the password manager","tool":"1Password","minutes":10,"done":false,"description":"Install 1Password on your laptop and phone, join the Northwind vault, and save your Emergency Kit somewhere offline.","detail":"Install from Self Service (macOS) or Company Portal (Windows), then sign in with the invite link. Turn on the browser extension for Chrome and Safari. Print or write down your Secret Key — IT cannot recover it for you. Move your SSO password into the 'Employee' vault and generate fresh 20-character passwords for any non-SSO tools.","owner":"IT Security","contact":"#it-security","guide":"https://it.northwind.io/guides/1password-setup"}}
{"op":"add","path":"/state/steps/2","value":{"id":"mfa","number":3,"title":"Enrol in 2FA (two factors, not one)","tool":"Okta Verify","minutes":8,"done":false,"description":"Register Okta Verify push on your phone plus one backup factor — either a YubiKey or SMS — so a lost phone never locks you out.","detail":"Go to okta.northwind.io > Settings > Extra Verification. Scan the QR code with Okta Verify and approve the test push. Then add a second factor: collect a YubiKey from the IT locker on floor 3 (preferred) or register your mobile number. Screenshot the recovery codes into your 1Password vault, not your camera roll.","owner":"IT Identity team","contact":"#it-helpdesk","guide":"https://it.northwind.io/guides/mfa-enrolment"}}
{"op":"add","path":"/state/steps/3","value":{"id":"vpn","number":4,"title":"Install the VPN and test a connection","tool":"GlobalProtect","minutes":12,"done":false,"description":"Connect to the corporate VPN and confirm you can reach an internal-only service such as the staging dashboard.","detail":"Install GlobalProtect from Self Service and set the portal to vpn.northwind.io. Sign in with SSO — it will trigger a 2FA push, so finish Step 3 first. Once connected, open dash.internal.northwind.io; if it loads, you're good. Keep 'Connect before logon' enabled so the VPN starts automatically on untrusted Wi-Fi.","owner":"Network Engineering","contact":"#network-ops","guide":"https://it.northwind.io/guides/vpn-globalprotect"}}
{"op":"add","path":"/state/steps/4","value":{"id":"encryption","number":5,"title":"Verify full-disk encryption is on","tool":"FileVault / BitLocker","minutes":15,"done":false,"description":"Confirm your disk is encrypted and that the recovery key has been escrowed to IT — this is an audit requirement.","detail":"macOS: System Settings > Privacy & Security > FileVault should read 'FileVault is on'. Windows: run 'manage-bde -status' in an admin terminal and check Conversion Status is 'Fully Encrypted'. If encryption is still in progress, leave the laptop plugged in until it completes. Then open the Kandji/Intune agent and confirm the compliance tile shows 'Recovery key escrowed'.","owner":"Endpoint Engineering","contact":"#it-endpoints","guide":"https://it.northwind.io/guides/disk-encryption-check"}}
{"op":"add","path":"/state/steps/5","value":{"id":"software","number":6,"title":"Install your role's software bundle","tool":"Self Service","minutes":20,"done":false,"description":"Install the Platform Engineering bundle: Slack, Zoom, Docker, VS Code, the Northwind CLI, and the observability agent.","detail":"Open Self Service and choose the 'Platform Engineering' bundle — it installs everything in one pass, roughly 20 minutes. Afterwards run 'nw doctor' in your terminal; it checks your CLI auth, Docker daemon, and kubeconfig and prints a green summary. Do not install developer tools via Homebrew until 'nw doctor' passes, or you'll end up with duplicate toolchains.","owner":"Developer Experience","contact":"#devex","guide":"https://it.northwind.io/guides/platform-bundle"}}
{"op":"add","path":"/state/steps/6","value":{"id":"channels","number":7,"title":"Join your team channels and groups","tool":"Slack + Google Groups","minutes":8,"done":false,"description":"Get added to #platform-infra, #platform-oncall, #incidents, #it-helpdesk, and the platform-eng@ mailing list.","detail":"Run '/onboard platform-infra' in Slack — the bot adds you to all required channels and the platform-eng@northwind.io group, and posts an intro on your behalf. Set your Slack display name to 'Priya R (she/her)' and upload a photo so on-call rotations are easy to read. Ask Marcus to add you to the PagerDuty shadow schedule; you won't be paged for the first four weeks.","owner":"Marcus Webb (IT Buddy)","contact":"#platform-infra","guide":"https://it.northwind.io/guides/team-channels"}}
{"op":"add","path":"/state/steps/7","value":{"id":"policy","number":8,"title":"Complete security training and sign the IT policy","tool":"Northwind Learn","minutes":15,"done":false,"description":"Finish the 12-minute security awareness module and acknowledge the Acceptable Use and Data Handling policies.","detail":"Open learn.northwind.io and complete 'Security Essentials — Day 1'. The phishing simulation at the end is graded; you need 80% to pass and can retake it immediately. Then e-sign the Acceptable Use Policy and Data Handling Standard. Access to production systems stays blocked until this step shows complete in your compliance dashboard.","owner":"Security & Compliance","contact":"#it-security","guide":"https://it.northwind.io/guides/security-essentials"}}
{"op":"add","path":"/elements/help-card","value":{"type":"Card","props":{"title":"Stuck on something?","description":"The three most common first-day snags and how to clear them."},"children":["help-accordion","help-actions"]}}
{"op":="add","path":"/elements/noop","value":{"type":"Text","props":{"text":""},"children":[]}}
{"op":"add","path":"/elements/help-accordion","value":{"type":"Accordion","props":{"type":"single","items":[{"title":"My activation link expired or won't load","content":"Links expire 72 hours after your start date. Don't request a password reset — instead post in #it-helpdesk with your full name and start date and IT will reissue the link within 15 minutes."},{"title":"VPN connects but internal sites still fail","content":"This is almost always a split-tunnel DNS issue. Disconnect, quit GlobalProtect fully, reconnect, then flush DNS (macOS: sudo dscacheutil -flushcache). If dash.internal.northwind.io still fails, share your GlobalProtect logs in #network-ops."},{"title":"Okta Verify push never arrives","content":"Check that notifications are enabled for Okta Verify and that your phone clock is set automatically — a clock drift over 30 seconds breaks the token. Use your backup factor to sign in, then re-enrol the push factor."},{"title":"FileVault says 'encryption in progress' for hours","content":"That's normal on a fresh laptop with a large disk. Keep it plugged in and awake; it typically completes in 1–3 hours. You can continue with Steps 6 and 7 while it finishes."}]},"children":[]}}
