{"op":"add","path":"/elements/rollback-alert","value":{"type":"Alert","props":{"title":"Trigger conditions","message":"Roll back immediately if 5xx rate exceeds 1% for 2 minutes, p99 latency doubles, health checks fail, or a pod enters CrashLoopBackOff. Do not debug forward in production.","type":"error"},"children":[]}}
{"op":"add","path":"/elements/rollback-why","value":{"type":"Text","props":{"text":"Rolling back the code is safe and fast because step 3 gave you an immutable previous image and step 5 kept the schema backward-compatible — the old version still runs against the new schema. That property is exactly why migrations must be additive: without it, a code rollback is impossible and you are forced into a database restore from step 4, which means downtime and data loss.","variant":"body"},"children":[]}}
{"op":"add","path":"/elements/rollback-cmd","value":{"type":"Text","props":{"text":"kubectl -n prod rollout undo deploy/api\nkubectl -n prod rollout status deploy/api --timeout=300

