### Validation notes

- Only allow-listed components used: `Column`, `Row`, `Card`, `Divider`, `Text`, `Icon`, `TextField`, `Button`.
- `updateComponents` emitted before `updateDataModel`, as required for non-DTO mode.
- Real `Button` + `action`, with a visible label `Text` and an explicit `background-color` — no fake buttons, no reliance on `variant` for color.
- All horizontal layouts have ≤ 3 children (`header_row` has 2).
- All binding paths use `/` separators; no dot notation; no dynamic `List` templates.
- One card shell only — `card_body` carries padding, never a second `background + border-radius + drop-shadow`; `root` handles layout and outer whitespace only.
- All sizes in `px`, `padding`/`margin` shorthands use four values, text styles applied only to `Text`, `filter` limited to `drop-shadow(...)`.
- No image URLs invented — the visual accent uses the built-in `mail` icon.

## Layout Rationale

**Mode:** Non-DTO Component (form card). Output order: `updateComponents` → `updateDataModel`.

- **Main sections (3):** ① Header (icon chip + title/subtitle) → ② Field group (name, email, message) → ③ Primary CTA + privacy footnote
- **Visual focal point:** the accent icon chip paired with the bold title at top, resolved by the solid blue CTA at the bottom
- **Content rhythm:** compact header → hairline divider → three evenly-spaced fields with a taller message area → full-bleed CTA → 24px trust footnote
- **Key horizontal relationships:** only two `Row`s, each with exactly 2 children (icon chip + text column; lock icon + note). Icon chips use `flex-shrink: 0`, text columns absorb compression. Fields stack vertically so labels can never be squeezed.
- **Role of images:** none. No fabricated image URLs — visual interest comes from a built-in `Icon` in a tinted chip.

**Improvement round applied:** the plain first draft (title + 3 fields + button) was upgraded for premium feel — added a single `Card` shell with soft elevation and outer whitespace, a tinted icon chip as a visual anchor, a hairline divider to separate header from inputs, a taller `longText` message field so it reads as a real text area, and a lock-icon privacy footnote for trust. CTA width is stretch-driven via `Column align: "stretch"` (never a fixed narrow width), so the label can never fragment.

