## Validation Self-Check

- ✅ **Component allowlist**: only `Column`, `Row`, `Card`, `Text`, `Icon`, `Divider`, `Table` — all in the catalog.
- ✅ **Card hard gate**: 3 main sections; no dynamic `List` sub-templates; no full-width hero image; no long body paragraphs.
- ✅ **Horizontal layout ≤ 3 children**: `header_row` has 2.
- ✅ **Single card shell**: one `Card`; `root` is layout-only with no background; no full visual shell on inner children.
- ✅ **Path binding**: all absolute paths use `/`, no dot notation; `updateDataModel.path` matches the binding prefix.
- ✅ **Font scale**: 36 / 28 / 24 only — all on the unified scale.
- ✅ **No fake buttons**: no clickable-looking element without a real `Button + action`; no CTA needed here, so none was invented.
- ✅ **Protected content**: numeric strings like `17,098,246` sit inside `Table` cells, not in a narrow fixed-width flex column, so no fragmentation risk.
- ✅ **Style whitelist**: `px` sizes only, four-value `padding`/`margin`, `border-style: solid`, `filter: drop-shadow(...)` only, no `gap`/`box-shadow`/`%`.
- ✅ **Height boundary**: header + 3-row table + footnote stays well under 1/3 screen height.

**Note on placeholders**: no image or link URLs were fabricated, so there is nothing you need to swap out before use.

## Layout rationale

- **Mode**: Non-DTO Component (no DTO provided, card requested) → `updateComponents` first, then `updateDataModel`.
- **Main sections (3, within budget)**: ① header (icon badge + title + subtitle) → ② the table (core deliverable, Tier‑2 structured component, explicitly requested) → ③ one-line footnote for measurement caveat.
- **Visual focal point**: the `Table` itself; the tinted icon badge acts as a small anchor so the header doesn't read as bare text.
- **Information rhythm**: compact header block, then the data grid, then a de-emphasized 24px footnote — descending weight, no competing visual centers.
- **Horizontal relationships**: only one `Row` (icon badge + text column, 2 children ≤ 3). Table is full-width, so no protected-column/CTA wrap risk.
- **Images/charts**: none — no real image URLs available, so nothing is fabricated. A `Chart` was considered but would push the card to 4 sections and compete with the user's explicit "table" request.
- **Improvement round applied**: first draft was title + table only; upgraded with an icon badge, a qualifying subtitle, a source/measurement footnote, and card elevation (border + drop-shadow + outer whitespace) for premium feel.

**Card hard gate**: sections 3 ✅ · no dynamic `List` templates ✅ · no full-width hero image ✅ · body paragraphs ≤ 2 ✅ · height ≪ 1/3 screen ✅

