## Notes before you ship

- **Replace the placeholder URL.** `cta_button` points at `https://status.example.com` — swap in your real status page, or drop the button entirely if you don't have one (remove `cta_button` from `card_body.children` and delete both `cta_button` and `cta_label`).
- **Card shape check:** 3 main sections, no dynamic `List` templates, no hero image, reassurance copy is a single short paragraph, every `Row` has exactly 2 children. Comfortably within card budget — this will not read as a page.
- **Amber, not red.** The accent palette (`#FFF7ED` / `#FED7AA` / `#B45309`) is deliberate: red styling would undercut

## Layout rationale

- **Main sections (3):** ① red alert band (icon + "FAILED" headline + status pill) → ② failure detail block (what broke, what to do) → ③ single retry CTA.
- **Visual focal point:** solid `#D32F2F` band with 40px bold white `FAILED` — highest contrast pairing available in the spec, plus a 3px red card border and a red-tinted drop shadow so the card reads as an alarm even in peripheral vision.
- **Information rhythm:** loud top → calm readable middle → one decisive action. No competing accents.
- **Key horizontal relationship:** `alert_band` is a 2-child Row — fixed-width icon chip (protected, `flex-shrink: 0`) + headline column (`flex-grow: 1`). `FAILED` is a protected short phrase and cannot fragment.
- **Role of images:** none. No image URLs fabricated; salience comes from the built-in `error` Icon on a white chip (Icon can't take `color`, so a white chip guarantees contrast).

**Improvement round applied:** first draft was a plain white card with red text. Upgraded to a full-bleed red alert band clipped by the card's `overflow: hidden`, added the status pill, and moved the detail copy into a tinted wash block — lightweight sectioning only, no card-in-card shell.

**On "flashing":** A2UI has no animation or keyframe primitives. The only animated component is `Lottie`, which requires a real asset URL — I won't invent one. If you have a hosted red-alert Lottie, drop the URL in and I'll swap the icon chip for it. Everything else here is maxed out: 40px is the top of the font scale, and white-on-red is the strongest contrast pair permitted.

Also note: I can't execute `validate_a2ui.py` in this channel. Manual gate check passed — 3 main sections, no dynamic List templates, no hero image, 2 body paragraphs, CTA in its own row (never sharing a Row with the pill), all horizontal layouts ≤ 3 children, all paths slash-separated.

