## Layout rationale (before JSON)

- **Mode**: Non-DTO Component (no DTO given, card is the default deliverable) → `updateComponents` first, then `updateDataModel`.
- **Main sections (3, at budget)**: ① solid-red alert band (icon + "FAILED"), ② what-went-wrong reason + status pills, ③ CTA row.
- **Visual focal point**: full-bleed `#D92D20` band with a white 112px icon disc and a 40px bold white `FAILED` — highest possible contrast in the first fixation.
- **Information rhythm**: heavy saturated block → calm white body → single decisive action row. Red-tinted `drop-shadow` lifts the whole card off the surface so it reads as an interrupt, not a list item.
- **Horizontal relationships**: icon disc is a protected column (`flex-shrink: 0`, fixed 112px); headline group absorbs all compression (`flex-grow: 1`). Pills sit on their own row, **separated from the CTA row** so no button can be pushed past the card edge. Every `Row` has exactly 2 children.
- **Role of images**: none — I will not fabricate image URLs. Semantic weight comes from the built-in `error` icon on a white disc (guarantees contrast, since `color` is a Text-only style and cannot be applied to `Icon`).

**Improvement pass applied**: first draft had the reason text and CTA on a plain white body with no chromatic tie-back. Revised to carry the red through a `#B42318` eyebrow label, `#FEE4E2` pills, and a red-tinted card border + glow — so severity persists after the eye leaves the band, instead of the alert "deflating" halfway down.

**On flashing**: A2UI has no keyframe, animation, or transition styles — `filter` is restricted to `drop-shadow(...)` only. Genuine flashing is only reachable via `Lottie`, which needs a real asset URL that I won't invent. Swap `cta_row`'s sibling in for a `Lottie` node if you have one; otherwise this maxes out static urgency.

