## Validation self-check

- **Card hard gate**: 3 main sections ✓ · no dynamic `List` templates ✓ · no full-width hero image ✓ · 1 body paragraph ✓ · height well under ⅓ screen ✓
- **Tag/CTA isolation**: `pill_row` and `cta_row` are separate `Column` siblings — no CTA clipping possible ✓
- **Row child limit**: every `Row` has exactly 2 children ✓
- **Single card shell**: `Card` owns background + radius + shadow; `card_body` adds none ✓ · `root` is layout-only with outer whitespace for the glow ✓
- **Real buttons**: both have `action` + visible label `Text`, with explicit `background-color` rather than relying on `variant` ✓
- **Protected columns**: icon disc `flex-shrink: 0`; buttons content-driven via `padding` + `flex-grow` (no narrow fixed width) — `Try Again` cannot break ✓
- **Style whitelist**: `px`-only sizes, four-value `padding`/`margin`, `filter` limited to `drop-shadow(...)`, text styles applied to `Text` only (no `color` on `Icon`) ✓
- **Font scale**: 40 / 32 / 28 / 24 ✓
- **Paths**: all absolute, `/`-separated ✓ · `surfaceId` matches across both messages ✓

**One thing to decide**: `retryFailedOperation` and `openFailureDetails` are event names I chose — wire them to your real handlers, or tell me the actual call signature (`functionCall` with args) and I'll swap them in.

## Layout rationale

**Mode:** Non-DTO Component (failure/alert card). No DTO given, no page requested.

- **Main sections (3):** ① alarm header (icon badge + "FAILED" + one-line subtitle) → ② one-paragraph failure summary + metadata chips → ③ action stack (primary Retry, secondary View log).
- **Visual focal point:** the whole card is inverted — solid deep red (`#C62828`) shell with a white circular icon badge punched into it. Inversion is the loudest thing A2UI can do without animation, and the white badge guarantees the `error` icon stays visible (Icon has no `color` style, so it must sit on a light chip).
- **Information rhythm:** 40px uppercase title → 28px subtitle → 32px body → 24px chips. Sharp size drop-off so the word "FAILED" wins the page.
- **Key horizontal relationships:** header = badge (protected, `flex-shrink: 0`, fixed 64px) vs. title block (compressible). Chips row is 2 short protected items with `flex-wrap: wrap`. Both CTAs are on **their own rows** — never beside the chips — so nothing gets pushed past the card edge.
- **Role of images:** none. Fabricating an image URL is not allowed and a hero image would turn this into a page header.

**Improvement round applied:** first draft was red text on a white card with the two buttons side-by-side in a `Row`. Upgraded to a fully inverted red shell (far higher alarm value) and split the two actions into separate rows to eliminate CTA clipping risk.

**On "flashing":** A2UI styles have no keyframes, `animation`, or `transition` — the only animating component is `Lottie`, which needs a real asset URL. I won't invent one. Give me a Lottie URL (a pulsing red alert loop) and I'll drop it in above the header as a 4th element.

