{"op":"add","path":"/elements/checklist","value":{"type":"Accordion","props":{"type":"multiple","items":[{"title":"Cost and commercial terms","content":"Model on-demand versus committed use, support charges, storage API calls, inter-AZ traffic, NAT gateways, backup, observability, marketplace licenses, and especially internet egress. Negotiate committed-spend discounts using a 3-year workload forecast."},{"title":"Resilience and uptime","content":"Do not equate a provider SLA with application availability. Design across availability zones, test regional failover, define RTO/RPO, and confirm service-specific SLA exclusions and service credits."},{"title":"Security and compliance","content":"Map each workload to required attestations, data residency, encryption key control, audit trails, identity federation, privileged access controls, and incident-response obligations. Compliance eligibility does not make an application compliant by itself."},{"title":"Performance and operations","content":"Benchmark cold starts, autoscaling, database latency, network paths, quotas, deployment speed, logging cost, and incident workflow. Include the availability of trained engineers and managed-service partners."}]},"children":[]}}

