{"op":"add","path":"/state/providers/0","value":{"id":"aws","rank":"#1 Overall","name":"Amazon Web Services (AWS)","fit":"Best for broad enterprise requirements, global products, and teams that need maximum service choice.","regions":"36 regions, 114 availability zones (announced and active footprint changes regularly).","uptime":"Most core services offer 99.9%–99.99% SLAs; multi-AZ architectures can target higher application availability.","pricing":"On-demand is generally competitive but complex. Savings Plans and Reserved Instances commonly reduce eligible compute spend by up to ~72% with 1–3 year commitments; Spot can reduce interruptible compute substantially.","egress":"Internet egress is commonly tiered and region-dependent; first 100 GB/month aggregated outbound is often free, then typical US ranges start around $0.09/GB and decline at volume. Cross-AZ and cross-region traffic can add material cost.","freeTier":"12-month introductory offers for selected services plus always-free quotas such as Lambda requests/compute, DynamoDB capacity, CloudWatch, and more.","support":"Basic included; Developer, Business, Enterprise On-Ramp, and Enterprise Support. Paid plans combine minimums and/or percentage-of-spend pricing; Enterprise includes concierge-style operational support.","coldStart":"Lambda: commonly ~100 ms to several seconds; Java/.NET and VPC-attached functions can be slower. Provisioned Concurrency reduces startup variability.","compliance":"Extensive certifications and programs: ISO, SOC, PCI DSS, HIPAA-eligible services, FedRAMP, GDPR tooling, and numerous regional frameworks.","strength":"Largest service portfolio, broadest ecosystem, mature infrastructure automation, strong multi-account governance.","watchout":"Pricing and IAM/networking concepts have a steep learning curve; cost controls must be designed early."}}
{"op":"add","path":"/state/providers/1","value":{"id":"azure","rank":"#2 Best Microsoft ecosystem choice","name":"Microsoft Azure","fit":"Best for Microsoft-centric enterprises, hybrid estates, regulated organizations, and Windows/SQL workloads.","regions":"More than 60 announced regions; one of the broadest geographic footprints, though availability-zone coverage varies by service and region.","uptime":"Typical service SLAs are 99.9%–99.99%; zonal or multi-region designs can improve application resilience.","pricing":"Pay-as-you-go, Reserved VM Instances, Savings Plan for Compute, spot pricing, and Azure Hybrid Benefit for eligible Windows Server/SQL Server licenses. Enterprise agreements can be decisive.","egress":"Outbound internet transfer is typically tiered by geography, often starting near $0.087–$0.12/GB in common zones after free allowances. Inter-zone and inter-region charges apply.","freeTier":"$200 introductory credit for eligible new accounts plus 12-month and always-free services with monthly limits.","support":"Basic included; Developer, Standard, Professional Direct, Unified Support, and enterprise agreements. Unified pricing is contract-specific.","coldStart":"Azure Functions: commonly hundreds of milliseconds to several seconds on Consumption; Premium and dedicated plans offer pre-warmed instances and lower variance.","compliance":"Very broad enterprise and public-sector portfolio including ISO, SOC, PCI, HIPAA, FedRAMP offerings, GDPR support, and sovereign cloud options.","strength":"Excellent identity integration with Entra ID, hybrid management via Azure Arc, and favorable licensing for Microsoft estates.","watchout":"Portal/service naming and overlapping product options can be confusing; regional feature parity varies."}}
{"op":"add","path":"/state/providers/2","value":{"id":"gcp","rank":"#3 Best data, AI, and cloud-native choice","name":"Google Cloud Platform (GCP)","fit":"Best for analytics, AI/ML, Kubernetes, modern data platforms, and teams prioritizing developer experience.","regions":"About 40 regions and 120+ zones, with a strong private backbone and continued expansion.","uptime":"Core service SLAs commonly range from 99.9% to 99.99% depending on topology and product.","pricing":"Per-second billing for many compute services, sustained-use discounts on eligible resources, committed-use discounts, and strong data/analytics pricing options. Evaluate BigQuery carefully by query and storage pattern.","egress":"Internet egress is destination- and service-dependent; common standard egress can begin around $0.12/GB, with lower-cost paths and special arrangements for some services/destinations.","freeTier":"$300 new-customer credit plus always-free quotas for selected Compute Engine, Cloud Run, Functions, BigQuery, storage, and other products.","support":"Basic included; Standard, Enhanced, and Premium Support. Higher tiers offer faster response targets, technical account assistance, and operational guidance.","coldStart":"Cloud Run often starts in hundreds of milliseconds to a few seconds depending on image/runtime; Cloud Functions can range similarly. Minimum instances reduce cold starts.","compliance":"Strong ISO, SOC, PCI, HIPAA-eligible service, FedRAMP, GDPR, and industry/regional compliance coverage.","strength":"BigQuery, Vertex AI, GKE, global networking, and a clean developer workflow are standouts.","watchout":"Smaller enterprise service catalog and partner market than AWS/Azure in some niches; fewer regions for strict locality needs."}}
{"op":"add","path":"/state/providers/3","value":{"id":"oci","rank":"#4 Best price/performance for Oracle workloads","name":"Oracle Cloud Infrastructure (OCI)","fit":"Best for Oracle Database and enterprise application estates, high-performance networking, and buyers able to negotiate committed contracts.","regions":"Around 50 commercial and government regions, with expanding distributed-cloud and dedicated-region options.","uptime":"Service SLAs vary, commonly 99.9%–99.99% for production services; architect across fault domains/availability domains where available.","pricing":"Often aggressive on VM, GPU, database, and outbound-transfer economics. Flexible shapes and universal credits can simplify some purchasing; negotiated enterprise terms matter significantly.","egress":"OCI is notable for a large outbound data-transfer allowance—commonly 10 TB/month free at account level—then lower published rates than many competitors in several regions.","freeTier":"Always Free services include select AMD/Arm compute, storage, database, monitoring, and a time-limited trial credit for new customers.","support":"Basic included; paid support plans such as Advanced Customer Services and Oracle Support Rewards-related programs vary by contract and product.","coldStart":"OCI Functions commonly experiences sub-second to several-second startup variation, depending on image size, language, and network setup; provisioned strategies reduce latency.","compliance":"Broad enterprise certifications including ISO, SOC, PCI DSS, HIPAA programs, FedRAMP-authorized offerings, and regional requirements.","strength":"Compelling economics for Oracle estates, fast networking, Autonomous Database, and generous transfer allowance.","watchout":"Smaller ecosystem, fewer managed-service choices, and fewer third-party integrations than the hyperscale top three."}}
{"op":"add","path":"/state/providers/4","value":{"id":"alibaba","rank":"#5 Best for China and Asia market access","name":"Alibaba Cloud","fit":"Best for China-focused deployments, Asian market coverage, and organizations that need local cloud capabilities in Alibaba’s ecosystem.","regions":"30+ regions and 80+ availability zones, with particularly strong China and Asia-Pacific coverage.","uptime":"Product SLAs commonly range from 99.9% to 99.99%; verify China-region SLA and service details separately.","pricing":"Pay-as-you-go, subscription, savings plans, reserved instances, and spot options. Pricing can be attractive in Asia but should be compared region by region.","egress":"Outbound internet pricing differs substantially by region and bandwidth model; pay close attention to China-region bandwidth, CDN, and cross-border routing charges.","freeTier":"Trial credits and limited free products are available, but eligibility and offers differ by country, account type, and campaign.","support":"Basic support plus paid Developer, Business, and Enterprise-style support offerings; response commitments and account coverage vary by plan and region.","coldStart":"Function Compute startup times are generally in the sub-second to several-second range depending on runtime, package/image size, VPC attachment, and reserved/provisioned instances.","compliance":"Supports major standards including ISO, SOC, PCI-related programs and regional certifications; confirm exact applicability for your target jurisdiction.","strength":"Strong local ecosystem and compliance pathway for China, plus broad Asia-Pacific reach and e-commerce-adjacent services.","watchout":"Cross-border operations, documentation/language, service parity, and geopolitical/data-residency requirements demand extra diligence."}}
