{"op":"add","path":"/elements/cost-notes-list","value":{"type":"Accordion","props":{"type":"multiple","items":[{"title":"Model the full bill of materials","content":"Include compute, managed databases, storage operations, logging, backups, NAT gateways, load balancers, observability, support, cross-zone traffic, inter-region replication, CDN, and internet egress."},{"title":"Test resilience and recovery","content":"Test a zone failure, a regional recovery path, backups, restore time, IAM break-glass access, and realistic RTO/RPO. A published service SLA is not an application SLA."},{"title":"Measure cold starts yourself","content":"Benchmark your exact runtime, deployment artifact, VPC configuration, secrets initialization, memory size, and concurrency. Use provisioned or minimum instances only where latency value outweighs idle cost."},{"title":"Negotiate after architecture is stable","content":"Commitment discounts can be valuable, but first baseline utilization and growth. Avoid long commitments for volatile workloads; prioritize portability and exit-aware data design."}]},"children":[]}}

