{"op":"add","path":"/state/providers/0","value":{"id":"aws","rank":"#1 overall","provider":"Amazon Web Services (AWS)","position":"Best all-purpose enterprise cloud","pricing":"Pay-as-you-go; Savings Plans and Reserved Instances commonly reduce steady compute spend by roughly 30–72%; Spot can be deeply discounted but interruptible.","regions":"33 geographic Regions and 105 Availability Zones publicly announced/available in the mid-2020s; broadest mature global footprint.","uptime":"Typical compute SLA: 99.99% for multi-AZ deployment patterns; individual service SLAs vary. Design across AZs and regions for stronger resilience.","compliance":"Extensive portfolio: ISO 27001, SOC, PCI DSS, HIPAA eligibility, FedRAMP, GDPR tooling, and many country/industry programs.","support":"Basic free; Developer, Business, Enterprise On-Ramp, and Enterprise Support. Business/Enterprise add 24×7 response and architectural guidance.","coldStart":"Lambda: often hundreds of milliseconds to several seconds, depending on runtime, package, VPC/networking, and initialization. Provisioned Concurrency can largely remove user-facing cold starts.","freeTier":"12-month introductory offers plus always-free quotas such as Lambda requests, DynamoDB capacity, and limited storage/service allowances.","egress":"Internet egress is generally charged by GB after a small monthly allowance; pricing is tiered and destination/service dependent. Same-region service paths can be cheaper or free depending on product.","services":"Deepest breadth: EC2, EKS, ECS, Lambda, S3, RDS/Aurora, DynamoDB, Redshift, Bedrock, SageMaker, analytics, networking, and security.","strengths":"Service breadth, partner ecosystem, global capacity, mature IAM/networking, strong multi-account governance.","watchouts":"Largest learning surface and a pricing model that needs active FinOps discipline."}}
{"op":"add","path":"/state/providers/1","value":{"id":"azure","rank":"#2 overall","provider":"Microsoft Azure","position":"Best for Microsoft, Windows, and hybrid estates","pricing":"Pay-as-you-go; Reserved VM Instances, Savings Plans, Azure Hybrid Benefit, and dev/test licensing can materially improve economics for Microsoft workloads.","regions":"60+ announced regions; exceptionally strong geographic coverage, with regional availability varying by service and capacity.","uptime":"Common VM SLA targets reach 99.99% when deployed across Availability Zones; product-specific SLAs and architecture requirements apply.","compliance":"Very broad enterprise and public-sector catalog: ISO, SOC, PCI, HIPAA eligibility, FedRAMP, GDPR support, and sovereign/government offerings.","support":"Basic free; Developer, Standard, Professional Direct, Unified support, and partner-led enterprise options.","coldStart":"Azure Functions consumption cold starts are commonly sub-second to several seconds; Premium/Dedicated plans and pre-warmed instances improve consistency.","freeTier":"$200 introductory credit for eligible new accounts plus always-free quotas for selected services, including limited Functions and storage/database offers.","egress":"Outbound internet data transfer is typically charged per GB after an allowance, with zone, destination, and service exceptions.","services":"Azure VMs, AKS, Functions, Blob Storage, SQL Database, Cosmos DB, Fabric/Synapse, OpenAI Service, Entra ID, Arc, and Windows Virtual Desktop.","strengths":"Best identity and licensing fit for Microsoft 365/Windows/SQL Server shops; strong hybrid management through Arc.","watchouts":"Portal and product overlap can be confusing; availability and maturity vary more noticeably by region/service."}}
{"op":"add","path":"/state/providers/2","value":{"id":"gcp","rank":"#3 overall","provider":"Google Cloud","position":"Best for data platforms, Kubernetes, and AI/ML teams","pricing":"Per-second billing for many compute services; committed-use discounts, sustained-use discounts on eligible compute, and flexible consumption models.","regions":"40+ regions and 120+ zones announced/available in the mid-2020s; fewer than Azure/AWS but strong in major markets.","uptime":"Typical Compute Engine SLA reaches 99.99% for qualifying multi-zone deployments; managed service SLAs differ.","compliance":"Major certifications including ISO, SOC, PCI, HIPAA eligibility, FedRAMP options, GDPR controls, and regional sovereignty offerings.","support":"Basic; Standard, Enhanced, and Premium Support packages, plus named technical account options at higher tiers.","coldStart":"Cloud Run cold starts are often low hundreds of milliseconds to seconds; min instances improve latency predictability. Cloud Functions behavior depends on generation/runtime.","freeTier":"$300 new-customer credit plus always-free usage for selected products such as a small Compute Engine instance in eligible US regions and Cloud Run quotas.","egress":"Internet egress is chargeable by destination and volume; Google offers some differentiated pricing and waivers for certain products/paths, but model it carefully.","services":"GKE, Compute Engine, Cloud Run, BigQuery, Cloud Storage, Spanner, Cloud SQL, Vertex AI, Pub/Sub, and strong data tooling.","strengths":"Excellent Kubernetes experience, BigQuery analytics, data engineering, networking, and AI platform capabilities.","watchouts":"Smaller enterprise application catalog and partner ecosystem than AWS/Azure in some verticals; egress still matters for multi-cloud designs."}}
{"op":"add","path":"/state/providers/3","value":{"id":"oci","rank":"#4 overall","provider":"Oracle Cloud Infrastructure (OCI)","position":"Best for Oracle Database and price-sensitive enterprise compute","pricing":"Competitive list pricing, flexible compute shapes, committed-use/Universal Credits, and strong commercial offers for Oracle workloads; compare effective contract pricing.","regions":"50+ public cloud regions announced/available, including commercial, government, and dedicated/sovereign options; service breadth may vary by region.","uptime":"Service SLAs commonly target up to 99.99% for qualifying highly available deployments; consult each OCI service commitment.","compliance":"Broad enterprise certifications: ISO, SOC, PCI, HIPAA eligibility, FedRAMP-authorized services in relevant regions, and data residency controls.","support":"Included Basic support; paid support levels and Oracle customer success/technical account services are contract dependent.","coldStart":"OCI Functions cold starts are workload/runtime dependent, generally comparable to other serverless platforms; provisioned or always-ready patterns reduce impact.","freeTier":"Always Free services include limited AMD/Arm compute, Autonomous Database capacity, object storage, and introductory credits for trials.","egress":"Notable differentiator: generous monthly outbound data-transfer allowance on many accounts before per-GB charges; exact terms and destinations matter.","services":"Autonomous Database, Exadata Cloud, OCI Compute, OKE, Functions, Object Storage, FastConnect, Analytics, and GenAI services.","strengths":"Compelling Oracle Database performance/licensing options, strong network economics, and attractive commercial positioning.","watchouts":"Smaller ecosystem and fewer managed-service choices than hyperscale leaders; validate regional service availability early."}}
{"op":"add","path":"/state/providers/4","value":{"id":"alibaba","rank":"#5 overall","provider":"Alibaba Cloud","position":"Best for China market access and Asia-focused digital commerce","pricing":"Pay-as-you-go and subscription/reserved models; competitive regional pricing, but currency, local entity, and product packaging affect comparisons.","regions":"30+ regions and 80+ availability zones globally, with a particularly strong mainland China footprint.","uptime":"Product SLAs vary; highly available architectures across zones are required to approach the highest stated commitments.","compliance":"Supports major standards such as ISO, SOC, PCI-related programs and regional compliance capabilities; assess jurisdiction-specific requirements with counsel.","support":"Free/basic entry support and paid support tiers with faster response, technical account, and enterprise services depending on geography and contract.","coldStart":"Function Compute cold starts vary by runtime, package size, VPC access, and traffic profile; reserved/provisioned capacity patterns help latency-sensitive services.","freeTier":"Free trials and promotional credits are commonly available; always-free entitlements and eligibility differ materially by country and account type.","egress":"Outbound internet transfer is generally metered by GB and varies by region, bandwidth model, and destination; model China cross-border traffic separately.","services":"ECS, ACK Kubernetes, Function Compute, OSS, ApsaraDB, MaxCompute, AI Platform, CDN, and extensive commerce-oriented services.","strengths":"Most practical major-cloud route to mainland China deployment, strong Asian presence, and Alibaba ecosystem alignment.","watchouts":"Documentation, support experience, contracting, and global service parity can differ from AWS/Azure/GCP; cross-border governance is complex."}}
