{"op":"add","path":"/elements/methodology-list","value":{"type":"Accordion","props":{"type":"multiple","items":[{"title":"Model total cost, not just compute","content":"Include compute commitments, managed databases, observability, support, backup, NAT gateways, load balancers, inter-zone traffic, internet egress, licensing, and people/operations cost."},{"title":"Test resilience claims","content":"Translate SLAs into an application design: multi-zone deployment, backups, recovery time and recovery point objectives, regional failover, dependency mapping, and regular game days."},{"title":"Validate regional reality","content":"Confirm that every required service, machine family, compliance scope, support response target, and capacity reservation exists in each target region."},{"title":"Benchmark your latency-sensitive paths","content":"Measure startup latency, database connection behavior, p95/p99 request latency, networking, and autoscaling under representative load. Cold-start figures are workload-dependent, not a provider constant."},{"title":"Treat compliance as a shared-responsibility program","content":"A provider certification does not certify your application. Map controls for identity, encryption, logging, retention, vulnerability management, data residency, and incident response."}]},"children":[]}}

