{"op":"add","path":"/state/recommendation","value":{"provider":"Amazon Web Services (AWS)","bestFor":"maximum service breadth, mature cloud-native teams, and global production workloads","summary":"AWS remains the strongest default when you need the widest infrastructure, data, AI, security, partner, and regional ecosystem in one platform.","reasons":"It has the deepest catalog, exceptionally broad global footprint, mature operational tooling, strong enterprise/compliance coverage, and the largest pool of experienced architects and managed-service partners. Its pricing is complex, but Savings Plans, Reserved Instances, Spot, Graviton, and FinOps tooling can produce excellent economics when actively managed.","caveat":"Choose Azure first when Microsoft identity, Windows Server, SQL Server, and Microsoft 365 dominate your estate. Choose Google Cloud first for analytics, Kubernetes, AI/ML, or exceptionally network-centric data platforms."}}
