{"op":"add","path":"/state/providers/0","value":{"id":"aws","rank":1,"name":"Amazon Web Services","score":"9.5","positioning":"The broadest general-purpose cloud platform and the safest default for complex, global, cloud-native estates.","bestFor":"service breadth, global scale, ecosystem depth, mature operations","watchout":"pricing complexity","regions":"36 geographic Regions worldwide (public cloud; count changes over time)","zones":"114+ Availability Zones","pricing":"On-demand is granular but can be expensive unmanaged. Savings Plans and Reserved Instances commonly reduce steady compute materially; Spot can discount interruptible capacity deeply. Graviton instances often improve price/performance.","uptime":"Service SLAs commonly range from 99.9% to 99.99%+ depending on product and multi-AZ architecture. Design across AZs and, where needed, Regions; no provider SLA replaces application resilience.","compliance":"Very broad portfolio: SOC 1/2/3, ISO 27001 family, PCI DSS, HIPAA eligibility, FedRAMP offerings, GDPR tooling, and extensive regional sovereignty controls.","support":"Basic included; Developer and Business percentage/minimum-fee plans; Enterprise On-Ramp and Enterprise Support for named guidance, faster response, and proactive operations.","coldStarts":"Lambda: typically hundreds of milliseconds to several seconds depending on runtime, package, VPC/network setup, and initialization. Provisioned Concurrency mitigates latency-sensitive paths.","freeTier":"12-month offers for selected services plus always-free quotas such as Lambda requests/compute; exact quotas and expiry vary by service and account program.","egress":"Often roughly US$0.09/GB for early internet-egress tiers in common US regions, declining at scale. Same-region service paths and CDN/cache design materially affect costs.","strengths":"EC2, EKS, Lambda, S3, RDS/Aurora, networking, security tooling, marketplace, partner network, specialized infrastructure, and worldwide operational maturity.","bottomLine":"Pick AWS if you value optionality, global production maturity, and the largest talent/partner pool—and can invest in landing-zone governance and FinOps."}}
{"op":"add","path":"/state/providers/1","value":{"id":"azure","rank":2,"name":"Microsoft Azure","score":"9.2","positioning":"The strongest choice for organizations deeply standardized on Microsoft identity, endpoints, databases, and productivity tooling.","bestFor":"Microsoft-centric enterprises, hybrid Windows estates, identity integration","watchout":"portal and service consistency","regions":"60+ announced/available regions, including extensive enterprise and government coverage","zones":"Availability Zones in many major regions","pricing":"Pay-as-you-go, Reserved VM Instances, Savings Plan for Compute, Azure Hybrid Benefit, and enterprise agreements. Existing Windows Server/SQL Server licenses can heavily change the economics.","uptime":"SLAs are service- and architecture-specific, commonly 99.9% to 99.99%+ for properly deployed services. Zone-redundant and multi-region designs improve resilience.","compliance":"Extensive enterprise, government, and industry attestations including SOC, ISO, PCI, HIPAA, GDPR, and broad FedRAMP/Azure Government options.","support":"Basic included; Developer, Standard, Professional Direct, and Unified Support options. Unified Support is generally negotiated for large Microsoft customers.","coldStarts":"Azure Functions cold starts vary by plan, language, dependencies, and networking. Consumption can be seconds; Premium plan pre-warmed instances and dedicated hosting reduce startup latency.","freeTier":"US$200 introductory credit in many markets plus selected always-free services/quotas; terms and availability are country- and program-dependent.","egress":"Common public internet egress benchmark is around US$0.087/GB for the first 5 TB/month in US zones, with volume tiers; routing and zone choices matter.","strengths":"Entra ID, Microsoft 365 integration, Windows/SQL modernization, Azure Arc, hybrid management, enterprise agreements, Power Platform, and strong developer tooling.","bottomLine":"Pick Azure when your Microsoft licensing, Entra identity, Windows/SQL footprint, or hybrid requirements create a clear operational and commercial advantage."}}
{"op":"add","path":"/state/providers/2","value":{"id":"gcp","rank":3,"name":"Google Cloud","score":"9.0","positioning":"A developer-friendly cloud with standout data, Kubernetes, AI, and network capabilities.","bestFor":"analytics, AI/ML, Kubernetes, data-intensive and cloud-native teams","watchout":"smaller enterprise service ecosystem","regions":"40+ regions and 120+ zones, with continuing expansion","zones":"120+ zones","pricing":"Per-second billing on many compute services, committed use discounts, Spot VMs, sustained-use discounts on eligible resources, and strong warehouse/serverless usage models. Compare carefully against workload shape.","uptime":"Product SLAs commonly range from 99.9% to 99.99%+; regional managed services and multi-zone GKE architectures are key for resilient designs.","compliance":"Broad SOC, ISO, PCI, HIPAA, GDPR, FedRAMP offerings, data-residency controls, encryption, Confidential Computing, and Security Command Center capabilities.","support":"Basic included; Standard, Enhanced, and Premium support with varying response targets, technical account management, and advisory services.","coldStarts":"Cloud Run can start quickly for small optimized containers but may range from sub-second to several seconds or longer for heavy images. Minimum instances reduce cold-start exposure; Cloud Functions behavior varies by generation/runtime.","freeTier":"US$300 trial credit for eligible new customers plus always-free quotas for selected products such as Cloud Run, Cloud Functions, BigQuery, and Compute Engine in specified regions.","egress":"Often about US$0.12/GB for initial standard internet egress in common North American tiers, with product, destination, CDN, and volume exceptions. Some strategic services differ.","strengths":"BigQuery, Vertex AI, GKE, Cloud Run, global networking, data engineering, open-source alignment, and excellent Kubernetes pedigree.","bottomLine":"Pick Google Cloud when data platforms, AI, Kubernetes, and developer velocity are central; validate regional coverage and partner availability for your operating countries."}}
{"op":"add","path":"/state/providers/3","value":{"id":"oracle","rank":4,"name":"Oracle Cloud Infrastructure","score":"8.0","positioning":"A compelling value and performance option, especially for Oracle database customers and predictable high-throughput workloads.","bestFor":"Oracle databases, Exadata, lower-egress architectures, price-sensitive enterprise compute","watchout":"smaller service and talent ecosystem","regions":"50+ commercial and government cloud regions, including distributed-cloud and dedicated-region options","zones":"Availability Domains and Fault Domains vary by region","pricing":"Competitive list pricing, flexible shapes, committed-use arrangements, and potentially strong Oracle license economics. Evaluate Universal Credits and support/licensing interactions closely.","uptime":"SLAs vary by service, commonly around 99.9% to 99.99%+ with higher targets for selected architectures. Use AD/fault-domain and multi-region design where required.","compliance":"Supports major standards including SOC, ISO, PCI, HIPAA programs, GDPR-related controls, and government/sovereign offerings in selected markets.","support":"Oracle Support plans and cloud support services are typically tied to agreement level; enterprise customers often engage dedicated account and technical resources.","coldStarts":"OCI Functions startup behavior depends on language, image size, dependencies, and concurrency. Expect seconds for cold paths unless provisioned/warmed patterns are used.","freeTier":"Always Free services include limited AMD/Arm compute, block/object storage, databases, and other quotas, plus time-limited trial credits for eligible accounts.","egress":"Notable differentiator: public messaging commonly includes a generous monthly outbound allowance, then competitive per-GB rates. Confirm current allowance and destination-specific terms.","strengths":"Autonomous Database, Exadata, Oracle application integration, bare metal, HPC/network performance, distributed cloud, and potentially favorable data-transfer economics.","bottomLine":"Pick OCI when Oracle workloads dominate, egress is large, or its commercial package beats hyperscaler pricing—while ensuring required managed services and skills are available."}}
{"op":"add","path":"/state/providers/4","value":{"id":"ibm","rank":5,"name":"IBM Cloud","score":"7.5","positioning":"A specialized enterprise platform with particular relevance for regulated industries, mainframe-adjacent estates, and hybrid operations.","bestFor":"regulated enterprises, Red Hat OpenShift, mainframe and hybrid modernization","watchout":"smaller hyperscale breadth","regions":"A global multi-zone region footprint with availability varying by service and country","zones":"Multi-zone regions plus single-zone locations","pricing":"Virtual server, bare metal, managed service, committed-use, and enterprise agreement pricing. Best evaluated with IBM/Red Hat platform and services requirements rather than raw VM list price alone.","uptime":"SLAs depend on service and deployment topology; multi-zone architecture and managed-service design are essential for higher availability targets.","compliance":"Strong heritage in regulated sectors, with broad security/compliance programs, financial-services focus, confidential computing options, and industry-specific governance capabilities.","support":"Support is offered through subscription and enterprise agreements, with varying severity response targets and premium account-management options.","coldStarts":"Code Engine and Functions startup latency depends on image/runtime size and scaling configuration; use small images and minimum instances where available for latency-sensitive services.","freeTier":"Lite plans and trial credits exist for selected services, including developer-oriented platform capabilities; quotas and regional eligibility vary.","egress":"Bandwidth charges vary substantially by service, location, and contract. Model outbound traffic explicitly; do not assume a single universal rate.","strengths":"Red Hat OpenShift, hybrid cloud consulting, mainframe integration, regulated-industry solutions, bare metal, and enterprise transformation services.","bottomLine":"Pick IBM Cloud when Red Hat hybrid operations, regulated-industry controls, or IBM/mainframe modernization are strategic—not as the broadest general-purpose hyperscaler."}}
{"op":"add","path":"/elements/methodology","value":{"type":"Card","props":{"title":"How to decide in practice","description":"The best provider is the one that minimizes total risk and operating cost for your specific workload—not necessarily the lowest VM price."},"children":["decision-accordion"]}}
{"op":"add","path":"/elements/decision-accordion","value":{"type":"Accordion","props":{"type":"multiple","items":[{"title":"Model total cost, not just compute","content":"Include storage operations, managed databases, observability, NAT/gateway processing, backups, support, enterprise discounts, licensing, inter-region traffic, internet egress, and people cost. Run a 12–36 month workload model with growth and commitment scenarios."},{"title":"Treat uptime as an architecture outcome","content":"Provider service SLAs are not an application availability guarantee. Set RTO/RPO, choose multi-AZ versus multi-region, test failover, quantify dependency failure modes, and design for identity, DNS, quota, and control-plane outages."},{"title":"Benchmark cold starts yourself","content":"Measure p50/p95/p99 startup latency using your exact runtime, package/image, VPC/network settings, secrets, dependencies, and traffic pattern. Provisioned/minimum instances trade idle cost for predictable latency."},{"title":"Validate compliance at service level","content":"A provider certification does not automatically make every workload compliant. Confirm the exact region, product, encryption/key model, audit evidence, data residency, subcontractors, and shared-responsibility controls."},{"title":"Negotiate after you know your demand shape","content":"Obtain comparable quotes only after right-sizing, commitment assumptions, support needs, and network topology are clear. Credits can obscure recurring costs; insist on effective-rate and renewal scenarios."}]}, "children":[]}}
{"op":"add","path":"/elements/next-step","value":{"type":"Card","props":{"title":"Recommended evaluation plan","description":"Shortlist AWS, Azure, and Google Cloud unless a specialized Oracle or IBM requirement is decisive."},"children":["evaluation-steps"]}}
{"op":"add","path":"/elements/evaluation-steps","value":{"type":"Stack","props":{"direction":"vertical","gap":"sm"},"children":["step-one","step-two","step-three","step-four"]}}
{"op":"add","path":"/elements/step-one","value":{"type":"Text","props":{"text":"1. Inventory workloads by latency, data gravity, compliance, operating system, database, and integration dependencies.","variant":"body"},"children":[]}}
